      <workList xml:id="workDesc_98c2a326">
         <work xml:id="work_id0d16ff7a">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_d1506fe1">C4:006</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_id88703738" xml:lang="de">Leben und Thaten des berühmten königlichen Dänischen Vice-Admirals, Peter Tordenschilds</title>
            <title type="original" xml:id="title_14d1b562" xml:lang="da">Den danske Søe-Heldt og Vice-Admiral Peder Tordenskiold omstændelige Livs og Heldte-Levnets Beskrivelse </title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_638b5a00">
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_id21f0d60c">Caspar Peter Rothe</persName>
               <persName role="translator" xml:id="persName_63cc0c35">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_id813d494f">
               <date isodate="1753" xml:id="date_00c300ac">1753</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id0383d484">
               <p xml:id="idm102">While living in Sønderborg, Scheibe translated the biography on the Danish naval hero, <persName xml:id="idm103" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peter Tordenskjold</persName>; the Danish version appeared in 1747–50. The project was extensive and comprised nearly 1,200 printed pages in all. As in many of his other translations Scheibe also in the present one included a foreword according to which he was commissioned by the publishers <persName xml:id="idm104" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Franz Christian Mumme</persName> some time ago. In order to cut printing expenses and to address a German audience, it was agreed with Mumme that the book should be revised and abridged. In April 1753 Scheibe signed his foreword and all three parts appeared later that year. Apparently a review of the present publication led to a discussion. The name of the translator does not appear in the book though the foreword is characteristic of Scheibe's style. However, in the short biography of Scheibe published in <rend xml:id="idm105" fontstyle="italic">Fortgesetzte Nachrichten</rend> of 1759, the translation is listed as being among one of his works.</p>
            </history>
